w": [3683, 42083], "confidence": 0.9, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Constrained temporal reachability from 1885 to 1460 with max_wait=600 fails: only 3 nodes are reachable at all and 1460 is not among them (step_01), and no time-respecting path is enumerable (step_09). Crucially, the failure is not merely a gap-length artifact \u2014 relaxing the waiting-time constraint entirely still yields no time-respecting route (step_02, 5 nodes reached), so the ordering of events, not the 600-unit budget, is the binding obstacle. Both of 1885's only out-neighbours (749, 1572) were tested as relay heads and neither reaches 1460 under the constraint (step_13, step_14), so no alternative first hop rescues the cascade. There is no direct edge in either direction (step_15). Confounder controls: the window is busy overall (7,194 events over 1,950 nodes, step_03), and the endpoints' neighbourhoods do share popular hubs such as 1132/1566 when time is ignored (step_05, step_11) \u2014 i.e. an order-agnostic connection plausibly exists \u2014 but that static adjacency does not translate into any temporally ordered chain. Likewise, the relays around 1460 (632, 765, 1045, 252) are moderately active (step_08) and the endpoint group's activity is spread across the window with no dead zone that would trivially explain the failure (step_12). Both endpoints are themselves low-degree (5 and 4 events, step_04). Verdict: connection exists structurally, cascade does not exist temporally."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_51debc25\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1885, 1460],\n  \"window\": [3683, 42083],\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Constrained temporal reachability from 1885 to 1460 with max_wait=600 fails: only 3 nodes are reachable at all and 1460 is not among them (step_01), and no time-respecting path is enumerable (step_09). Crucially, the failure is not merely a gap-length artifact \u2014 relaxing the waiting-time constraint entirely still yields no time-respecting route (step_02, 5 nodes reached), so the ordering of events, not the 600-unit budget, is the binding obstacle. Both of 1885's only out-neighbours (749, 1572) were tested as relay heads and neither reaches 1460 under the constraint (step_13, step_14), so no alternative first hop rescues the cascade. There is no direct edge in either direction (step_15). Confounder controls: the window is busy overall (7,194 events over 1,950 nodes, step_03), and the endpoints' neighbourhoods do share popular hubs such as 1132/1566 when time is ignored (step_05, step_11) \u2014 i.e. an order-agnostic connection plausibly exists \u2014 but that static adjacency does not translate into any temporally ordered chain. Likewise, the relays around 1460 (632, 765, 1045, 252) are moderately active (step_08) and the endpoint group's activity is spread across the window with no dead zone that would trivially explain the failure (step_12). Both endpoints are themselves low-degree (5 and 4 events, step_04). Verdict: connection exists structurally, cascade does not exist temporally.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 52801, "total_output_tokens": 3908, "total_tokens": 56709, "total_latency_ms": 58045, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}